cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this note or its computations, please cite it as below.
  Please also cite the OpenAI preprint listed in UPSTREAM.md.
type: software
title: "An explicit isoperimetric constant for Thompson's group F"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-10'
authors:
  - name: '[AUTHOR NAME]'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  OpenAI's preprint proves that Thompson's group F is nonamenable, but gives no
  explicit isoperimetric constant. Tracking every constant of that argument for
  the standard generators x0, x1, we prove that the edge-isoperimetric (Cheeger)
  constant h_E(F) = inf_A (|x0 A - A| + |x1 A - A|)/|A| (symmetric differences)
  is at least 2.109e-19, and at least 2.466e-19 with a sharper word-length
  lemma. If the Hilbert unit ball admits a k-Lipschitz retraction onto its
  sphere, then h_E(F) >= g(k) for an explicit g, with g(29) = 8.596e-9. This is
  a standard effectivization with no new mechanism; one step is
  computer-assisted and not formalized, and the result is conditional on the
  correctness of the upstream preprint. Found and checked by Claude (Anthropic)
  agents under the repository owner's direction. No human peer review has taken
  place and nothing here is formalized in Lean.
keywords:
  - Thompson's group F
  - nonamenability
  - isoperimetric constant
  - Cheeger constant
  - explicit bounds
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Thompson's group F is nonamenable"
    authors:
